            "review_text": "RayAnh72\nHong Kong, China630 contributions\n0\nConfidential seafood\nSep 2016\nThis rooftop place has the feel of a Delta village shack, complete with minute wooden chairs, banana trees and country earthenware. But the numerous young and well-off local clients come here for seriously good seafood: an amazing array of snails, clams, etc., all perfectly fresh and competently cooked with lemongrass bouillon and other flavors. As welcome snack, we got guava (served with salt and chili) and quail eggs (beware, they are hatched – definitely an acquired taste). It helps to speak Vietnamese but even then, unless you are a sea biology teacher, you are unlikely to recognize all the names on the menu. We hear that pictures are available on their Facebook site, but we got advice from our waitress. Getting there is part of the fun. No name in the street, go to the end of the small alley under the sign “Papa Café”. Once there, take the stairs on your left (still no name). On the second floor, you’ll find rickety red iron steps under a sign “Oc Chi Em”.\nRead more\nWritten September 24, 2016",
